 r←Test_Misc_025(stopFlag batchFlag);⎕TRAP;parms;Resolve
⍝ Checks how `ResolveReadmeLinks` resolves the links of a rendered README.
⍝ In particular one that starts with a "/": GitHub renders a README at github.com, so a
⍝ browser resolves such a link against that origin rather than against the repository.
⍝ Resolved the other way it was left pointing at us and answered with a 404.
 ⎕TRAP←(999 'C' '. ⍝ Deliberate error')(0 'N')
 r←T._Failed

 parms←'aplteam' 'APLGit2' 'v1.2.0'
 Resolve←##.Server.ResolveReadmeLinks

⍝ Site relative: the path is kept as it is, and github.com is put in front of it
 →T.PassesIf'href="https://github.com/aplteam/Tatin"'≡parms Resolve'href="/aplteam/Tatin"'
 →T.PassesIf'src="https://github.com/aplteam/Tatin/raw/main/pic.png"'≡parms Resolve'src="/aplteam/Tatin/raw/main/pic.png"'

⍝ Relative to the repository: resolved against the tag the README came from
 →T.PassesIf'href="https://github.com/aplteam/APLGit2/blob/v1.2.0/docs/x.md"'≡parms Resolve'href="docs/x.md"'
 →T.PassesIf'src="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/aplteam/APLGit2/v1.2.0/pic.png"'≡parms Resolve'src="./pic.png"'

⍝ Left alone
 →T.PassesIf'href="https://example.com/x"'≡parms Resolve'href="https://example.com/x"'
 →T.PassesIf'href="#foo"'≡parms Resolve'href="#foo"'

 r←T._OK
⍝Done
